  "facts": [
    "The Harlem River Lift Bridge, completed in 1956, can lift its 340‑foot spans in just four minutes, a dramatic improvement over the 1897 swing bridge that delayed trains nine minutes per opening.",
    "When closed, the bridge offers 25 feet of clearance, but opens to a staggering 135 feet, allowing even the largest naval vessels to pass beneath.",
    "During the 2014‑2015 renovation, the bridge’s motors, circuit breaker room, and counterweight cables were entirely replaced, restoring reliability after a Hurricane Sandy‑induced flood."
